WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.384 --> 00:00:03.134
(dramatic music)

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.170
- There's this house in this
neighborhood in New Jersey

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.300
that actually isn't a house.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.250
It's hard to see, because
it's behind this gate,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.140
but if you look at it from above,

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.810
you'll see that it's actually
a really large building.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.490
Kind of looks like a warehouse.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.710
It has dozens of air conditioning units

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.720
and it's just sitting here among a sea

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.523
of ordinary suburban homes.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.350
All of this is just a facade
hiding this massive building

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.140
that is a landing station for AT&amp;T,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.720
the place where these
massive undersea cables

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.885
that connect the world,
hit the eastern seaboard.

00:00:36.885 --> 00:00:40.320
(suspenseful music)

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.690
We now know for certain
that the U.S. government

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.710
spies on those cables with the
help of companies like AT&amp;T.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.170
And according to a
leaked map from the NSA,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.540
they process all the
data that they collect

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.740
somewhere in New Jersey in
a facility called Pinecone.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.290
Lining up these maps points to this

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.950
secretive disguised building
as one of the best candidates

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.590
for where this surveillance
is being processed.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.240
But there's a lot more
of these hidden buildings

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.380
around the country.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.150
Thanks to leaked NSA documents

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.130
and some thorough investigative reporting,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.200
we now know some of their locations.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.910
Like the fake house in New Jersey,

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.640
these other cable spy facilities blend in

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.890
as benign, nondescript buildings

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.720
avoiding any undue attention

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.413
along the streets of New York
or San Francisco or Dallas.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.400
These few hundred cables
that connect our world

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.860
contain an unfathomable amount of data,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.890
all of our communication,
all of our connections,

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.920
and it would seem impossible
that any government agency

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.990
would be able to spy on it all,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.870
impossible, that is, if
we didn't have solid proof

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:43.803
that they do.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.880
So let me tell you the story of the cables

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.650
that connect our planet

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.050
and show you that if
you can tap into them,

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.050
you can watch the world and they have,

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.660
and they've been doing it for a long time.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.880
- [Reporter 1] 320
million records every day.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.080
- [Reporter 2] What
we're talking about here

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.520
is a total revolution

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.090
of the whole concept of war.
- Collect it all,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.692
exploit it all.

00:02:07.692 --> 00:02:10.500
(TV static)

